interface @beta Efl.Ui.Legacy
{
   [[Marker interface for widgets instantiated through the legacy $[elm_*_add()]
     API.

     Widget classes are shared between the unified and the legacy API, so a class
     alone does not say which of the two created a given object. Legacy widget
     classes therefore implement this interface and nothing else: it declares no
     methods, no properties and no events, and exists purely so that
     $[efl_isa(obj, EFL_UI_LEGACY_INTERFACE)] can answer that question. Widget
     code asks through $[elm_widget_is_legacy()] and uses the answer to pick the
     legacy theme group name, the legacy part aliases and the compatibility
     behaviour paths.

     This is internal machinery. Applications should not implement it, and its
     presence on an object is not part of any API contract.
   ]]
}
